The largest change across allocation methods is {{ m.largest_method_move.range_micro|money }}. An allocation policy changes who pays without changing the total. Idle capacity is therefore reported separately before overhead is distributed.

The FinOps objection is valid: list prices do not equal a negotiated invoice. This report uses recorded price excerpts and labels the scenario. Portfolio usage remains not measured until the authenticated fetch has run.

